<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Exits</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>exits</a>
<a cmd='#'>directions</a>
<a cmd='#'>doors</a>
</pre>
<p>All three list the obvious exits of the room you are in: each direction, and the 
place it leads to, or the door that is closed that way. Click a direction to 
walk there. Hidden and secret exits aren't shown; you have to find those 
yourself. In the dark you see no exits at all, only that it is pitch black.
</p><p><a cmd='#'>change exits</a> switches on and off whether you see the exits by themselves 
every time you walk into a room.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Change</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Doors</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Enter</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Movement</a>
</pre>




</div>